Recommends: ${apklayer:Recommends}, mesa-utils, pkexec, xdg-utils, desktop-file-utils,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-libav
Description: run Android apps on Linux in Wayland windows
 apklayer runs Android apps (APKs) as Linux processes: the app's dex code is
 converted to JVM classes once, Android's own native libraries run through
 bionic_translation, and each app opens a Wayland window. This package holds
 the command line tool, the window shell, the native runtime and
 apklayer-manager; the Android runtime bundle (Android's libraries and
 framework) is downloaded per user by apklayer-manager.
